  "conclusion": "Register lowering substantially reduces BINARY64 executed instructions but full per-op AOT plus duplicate fast code does not fit Classic. Keep this as an isolated PoC, not a deployment.",
  "next_direction": "Compact bytecode for cold code/deoptimization and a bounded selected-hot-block ARM working set; native cache/loader/emitter/relocation cost and hot-set coverage still unmeasured.",
  "limitations": [
    "all old cold native per-op labels retained; this is not a minimum-size typed compiler",
    "fixed-address native research ELF, no relocatable native APP or on-device compilation",
    "ARM target performance is BINARY64; CORE has host semantic/chess checks only and no demonstrated speedup",
    "no source/filesystem/OPEN/decompression, USB or physical keyboard latency in this fixture",
    "GRAPH expression plotting remains rejected; ordinary graphics events tested",
    "unboxed SSA does not prohibit compiler spills; static frame sizes are not stack high-water"
  ],
